# Database Table Names

## Rule

Physical database **table names must be camelCase**, not PascalCase or snake_case.

- Use Prisma `@@map("tableName")` so the SQL table is camelCase even when the Prisma model is PascalCase.
- Prefer plural or compound names when needed (e.g. `users`, `workflows`, `workflowMetadata`).
- Do **not** create or rename tables to PascalCase (`User`, `Workflow`).

## SQLite note

SQLite table names are case-insensitive, so `User` and `user` collide. Prefer plural/compound camelCase (`users`, `workflowMetadata`) instead of single-word lowercasing of a PascalCase model name.

## Examples

```prisma
// ❌ BAD — default PascalCase table "User"
model User {
  id String @id
}

// ✅ GOOD
model User {
  id String @id
  @@map("users")
}

model WorkflowMetadata {
  id String @id
  @@map("workflowMetadata")
}
```

Document table name choices in `docs/technology.md` when the schema changes.
